{"requirements":[{"id":"shared-writable-directory","requirement":"On node1, /srv/drop exists as a shared directory writable by unprivileged users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"/srv/drop was created as root:root with mode 1777. Two distinct unprivileged accounts successfully created files, and the same behavior was directly reverified after node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-af092f8d23e84da5","cmd-c1606ad85b6b449e","cmd-24d764d3953549f1","cmd-59a3476abf31400a"]},{"id":"foreign-file-removal-protection","requirement":"Users cannot remove files in /srv/drop that are owned by other users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The directory has the sticky bit, and daemon's attempts to remove nobody's file were rejected with Operation not permitted both before and after restart; the foreign-owned file remained present.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c1606ad85b6b449e","cmd-59a3476abf31400a"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: creating the required directory, performing bounded permission tests with cleanup, and executing the mandatory restart protocol. Test files were removed, no failed services or new listeners remained, and package health was intact. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutation was observed. The sole hygiene defect is the retained /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log created by the restart command; it remained after execution as minor temporary-file residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-af092f8d23e84da5","cmd-c1606ad85b6b449e","cmd-e135447b2353494a","cmd-59a3476abf31400a","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. Direct behavior tests establish shared write access and sticky-bit protection, and both properties survived a confirmed node restart. The restart protocol is coherent: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered directory behavior; lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["Behavior was sampled with two unprivileged system accounts rather than every possible local user, though mode 1777 and repeated direct tests provide strong general evidence.","The retained /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log is minor executor-created residue."]}
